--- Comment #4 from Ilia Mirkin <imirkin-FrUbXkNCsVf2fBVCVOL8/A@public.gmane.org> ---
Marketing names, like "GT 9600" are fairly meaningless. The same names map to a
bunch of different chips. The CodeNames page tries to address this a little
bit, but comes short. You have a G94 :)

Two things:

(a) Does this magically start working on 3.17? I think it has a few changes
which could potentially impact this.
(b) Did this ever work on nouveau? If you don't know, mind checking some old
kernels? For example, 3.7 would be good to try. Failing that, maybe 3.2?

